The sparse n-gram selection algorithm implemented in
crates/pixel-index/src/gram.rs is an independent Rust implementation of
the algorithm described publicly by ClickHouse (src/Functions/sparseGramsImpl.h,
Apache-2.0) and by Cursor ("Fast regex search: indexing text for agent tools").
No ClickHouse source code was copied.

## Bundled / transitive dependencies

This project bundles or depends on the following notable components:

- **SQLite** (Public Domain) — bundled via the `rusqlite` crate's
  `bundled` feature. Source: https://www.sqlite.org/
- **OpenSSL** (Apache-2.0) — vendored via the `openssl` crate's `vendored`
  feature, compiled from source at build time. Required transitively by
  `fastembed` → `hf-hub` → `native-tls`. Source: https://www.openssl.org/
- **ONNX Runtime** (MIT) — downloaded as prebuilt binaries by the
  `fastembed` crate for neural embedding inference. The runtime is loaded
  at build/run time, not compiled into the binary. Source:
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
- **option-ext** (MPL-2.0) — used for `Option::unwrap_or` extensions.
  Source: https://github.com/servo/rust-option-ext
- **Tree-sitter grammars** (MIT, all 8) — used for code graph parsing:
  tree-sitter, tree-sitter-typescript, tree-sitter-javascript,
  tree-sitter-rust, tree-sitter-go, tree-sitter-java, tree-sitter-python,
  tree-sitter-c. Source: https://github.com/tree-sitter/
- **Embedding models** — downloaded from Hugging Face Hub on first use
  via `pixel recall setup` (the pixel-recall plugin):
  - Multilingual E5 Small (fastembed default)
  - potion-base-2M (model2vec)
  These models have their own licenses; see the Hugging Face model pages.

- **Microsoft Pragmatic Rust Guidelines** (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft
  Corporation) — the concatenated agent text `src/agents/all.txt` is
  vendored verbatim as `.agents/skills/rust-guidelines/guidelines.txt` for
  coding agents working on this repository; it is not part of the binary.
  Source: https://github.com/microsoft/rust-guidelines
- **Apollo GraphQL `rust-best-practices` skill** (MIT, Copyright (c)
  Apollo Graph, Inc.) — the borrowing, type-state, TODO, test-naming and
  snapshot-testing points in `.agents/skills/rust-guidelines/SKILL.md` are
  restated from it in this repository's own words; no text is vendored.
  Source: https://github.com/apollographql/skills/tree/main/skills/rust-best-practices

No GPL or AGPL licensed components are used anywhere in this project.
